  "notes": "FORMS:\n{狼狽|ろうばい}する - to be flustered, to panic\n\nETYMOLOGY:\nFrom Chinese. {狼|ろう} (wolf) and {狽|ばい} (legendary wolf-like creature) were said to be inseparable. When apart, both would panic - hence the meaning of confusion.\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {慌|あわ}てる - to panic, to be flustered (more common)\n- {動揺|どうよう}する - to be shaken, disturbed\n- うろたえる - to be confused, lose composure\n\nUSAGE:\n{狼狽|ろうばい} is more literary and formal than {慌|あわ}てる.",
